## 🧩 1️⃣ `uppercase.directive.ts`

```typescript
import { Directive, ElementRef, AfterViewInit } from '@angular/core';

// 👇 Custom Directive Definition — appUppercase
@Directive({
  // Selector name — you’ll use this as an attribute in HTML like [appUppercase]
  selector: '[appUppercase]'
})
export class UppercaseDirective implements AfterViewInit {
  
  // ElementRef gives direct access to the host DOM element
  constructor(private el: ElementRef) {}

  // ngAfterViewInit() lifecycle hook runs after the element is loaded in the DOM
  ngAfterViewInit() {
    // Get the current text inside the element
    const text = this.el.nativeElement.innerText;

    // Convert that text content to uppercase
    this.el.nativeElement.innerText = text.toUpperCase();

    // Log message to confirm the directive executed
    console.log('UppercaseDirective works — text converted to UPPERCASE');
  }
}
```

💡 **What it does:**  
Whenever you use `[appUppercase]` on an element, any text inside it automatically becomes **UPPERCASE** once it renders.

**Example:**
```html
<p appUppercase>hello world</p>
<!-- Output on screen: HELLO WORLD -->
```

