## 🧩 4️⃣ `login.service.ts`

```typescript
import { UserService } from './user.service';

// Service responsible for user login functionality
export class LoginService {
  
  // 👇 Dependency Injection — this pulls in an instance of UserService
  constructor(private userService: UserService) {
    console.log('LoginService Initialized Successfully');
  }

  // Method to simulate user login
  userLogin() {
    // Get user details from UserService
    const user = this.userService.getUserInfo();

    // Log a simulated login process
    console.log('Logging in user...');

    // Prints user’s name and role + login timestamp
    console.log(`${user.name} (${user.role}) logged in successfully at ${new Date().toLocaleString()}`);
  }
}
```

💡 **What it does:**  
Simulates a login process by fetching user info and printing it with the current time.

